From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop: no cursor plane on the PX30's big VOP

SDL's KMSDRM backend draws its default cursor on a CRTC's cursor plane
at start, mouse or not, so every SDL app on the R36H showed an arrow in
the top left corner. A handheld has no use for it, and the Allwinner
consoles this rootfs also runs on have no cursor plane either: the
window is offered as an overlay instead.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
index 72301e0a3..4eec4292e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@ static const struct vop_win_data px30_vop_big_win_data[] = {
 	{ .base = 0x00, .phy = &px30_win1_data,
 	  .type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY },
 	{ .base = 0x00, .phy = &px30_win2_data,
-	  .type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR },
+	  .type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY },
 };
 
 static const struct vop_data px30_vop_big = {
